==Pre-match==

===Identity===
The original identity of the 2024 UEFA Europa Conference League final was unveiled at the group stage draw on 1 September 2023.<ref>{{Cite web |date=1 September 2023|title=2024 UEFA Europa League and UEFA Europa Conference League final identities revealed |url=https://www.uefa.com/news-media/news/0285-18df8e6abdf2-f54ceb925270-1000--2024-uefa-europa-league-and-uefa-europa-conference-league-fi/ |access-date=2 September 2023|website=UEFA.com|publisher=Union of European Football Associations}}</ref>

===Ticketing===
The stadium has a capacity of 32,500, and 27,100 were made available of which 21,000 were on sale to the general public. Each club in the final received an allocation of 9,000 tickets each.<ref>{{cite web | last=Calcutt | first=Robert | title=12k fans for each side in Europa League final and 25k fans at 90k Wembley | website=talkSPORT | date=9 April 2024 | url=https://talksport.com/football/1820311/uefa-tickets-prices-allocation-champions-league-europa-league-europa-conference-league-finals/ | access-date=27 May 2024}}</ref>

==Match==
===Summary===
After a goalless ninety minutes, the match went into extra-time. In the 116th minute Olympiacos went in front when [[Ayoub El Kaabi]] got the only goal of the match when he stooped low to head the ball into the left corner of the net after a cross from the left by [[Santiago Hezze]].<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.theguardian.com/football/article/2024/may/29/olympiakos-fiorentina-europa-conference-league-final-match-report|title=Olympiakos win Europa Conference League after El Kaabi floors Fiorentina|date=29 May 2024|work=The Guardian|accessdate=30 May 2024}}</ref> After a lengthy [[Video assistant referee|VAR]] check the goal was eventually awarded and Olympiacos went on to win their first European trophy.<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/live/c988jy177gqt|title=Olympiakos 1 Fiorentina 0|date=29 May 2024|work=BBC Sport|accessdate=30 May 2024}}</ref>

===Details===
